# $showProperties(pRef[,pIsList=kFalse,pToFront=kTrue]) -> Boolean
# Feeds the Property Manager with pRef (core, undocumented, reverse
# engineered from the IDE shell). Returns kTrue if shown, kFalse if the
# Property Manager panel is not visible (nothing done then).
#
# Core commands used:
#   $dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,47) = PREPARE, ensures panel exists
#   $dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,46) = ISVISIBLE, gate before feeding
#   $dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,1,ref,isList,toFront) = SHOW
#
# pRef: any notation reference (class, object, group, $prefs, instance).
# pIsList=kTrue: pRef is a LIST of objects (multi-selection) — itemrefs
#   must sit in COLUMN 5, rows to show must be $selected=kTrue
#   (shell pattern: Do list.$define(,,,,item) + $sendall select).
# pToFront=kTrue brings the panel to front.
#
# Note: runtime properties render green regardless of pRef being a live
# instance — that is a PM display state (context menu: Show Runtime
# Properties), not controllable by parameter.
# See also $clearProperties. Source: oDatafiles/oLibraries doprops @2026
Do $root.$modes.$dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,47) Returns ret ## prepare @CORE
Do $root.$modes.$dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,46) Returns ret ## visible? @CORE
If ret
	Do $root.$modes.$dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,1,pRef,pIsList,pToFront) ## @CORE
End If
Quit method ret